From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shlwapi: ordinal 615 is SHCreateThreadWithHandle

SHCreateThreadWithHandle is documented as shlwapi ordinal 615, and OneDrive's shell extension imports it by that ordinal. Wine did not export it from shlwapi, and the named exports it numbers from 552 put PathIsLFNFileSpecA at 615, so OneDrive's overlay handler started no thread and waited for it forever. shlwapi now exports SHCreateThreadWithHandle at 615, forwarded to shcore.
---
diff --git a/dlls/shlwapi/shlwapi.spec b/dlls/shlwapi/shlwapi.spec
index 56839df..fd543ca 100644
--- a/dlls/shlwapi/shlwapi.spec
+++ b/dlls/shlwapi/shlwapi.spec
@@ -545,6 +545,9 @@
 549 stdcall -noname SHCoCreateInstanceAC(ptr ptr long ptr ptr)
 550 stub -noname GetTemplateInfoFromHandle
 551 stub -noname IShellFolder_CompareIDs
+# Stained Glass OS 6252: SHCreateThreadWithHandle is ordinal 615 (documented; OneDrive's shell extension
+# imports it so). Wine's named exports were numbered from 552 and PathIsLFNFileSpecA got 615.
+615 stdcall -ordinal SHCreateThreadWithHandle(ptr ptr long ptr ptr) shcore.SHCreateThreadWithHandle
 
 @ stdcall AssocCreate(int128 ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall AssocGetPerceivedType(wstr ptr ptr ptr)
